-- Equity Uprise: paying with a share of revenue instead of cash (5 chunks)
insert into public.kb_documents (org_id, kind, url, title, body, source, content_hash, enabled)
select o.id, 'program', 'https://matthew.mccluster.org/sites-details.html#equity', 'Equity Uprise: paying with a share of revenue instead of cash', 'No stock. No membership interest. No ownership. Equity Uprise is a time-limited revenue-share agreement. Revenue sharing ends at the earlier of the stated term or the stated cap, whichever comes first. The domain is always paid separately, up front. Participation requires a program-fit review and a signed agreement.

## What it is
Half the standard monthly price, against a capped share of the revenue the
work actually brings in. It is a payment arrangement, not an investment: no
ownership is taken and no equity in the company changes hands, whatever the
name suggests.

## The numbers on Anti-Social
$437.50 a month, plus 50% of approved eligible connected online revenue, for up to 12 months, ending at the earlier of the term or a $105,000 cap.

## Which services have it
Anti-Social has an approved Equity Uprise rate. Who Did the Shoot and Write a
Song are quoted per project, so an arrangement for those is written during
discovery and there is no standing formula. Domain and hosting has none at all.

## It is an agreement, not a button
Equity Uprise cannot be bought in a tap because it is a contract. It starts at
https://matthew.mccluster.org/onboard.html and the terms are written down before anything begins.
', 'ledger', '1227:14609146', true
  from public.orgs o where o.slug = 'mccluster'
on conflict (org_id, kind, coalesce(url, title)) do update
  set title = excluded.title, body = excluded.body,
      content_hash = excluded.content_hash, enabled = true, updated_at = now();

